$schema: changelog.schema.eure

base = "a6982fb2d139322d9bf84a54eaa40fa18415ddad"
summary = ````markdown
Exported functions of the JavaScript backend may use a `Ref`, a `Weak`, a `Mutex`, an `Atomic` and `hash_seed`; and two fixes: `tauto check` on a tote whose test body, in a file that is not the entry, calls a function with an effect indexed by a type, and the JavaScript backend's copy of a host object bound by a handler arm.
````

@ fixed[]
area = "effects"
summary = ````markdown
`tauto check` accepts a tote in which a file that is not the entry calls, in the body of a `perform test(...)`, a function with an effect indexed by a type (`context(A)`).
````
details = ````markdown
The call gets the copy the effect's type asks for, as it does when the file is the only one of the tote; adding an unrelated file to the tote does not change the result.
````

@ fixed[]
area = "backends"
summary = ````markdown
The JavaScript backend keeps the contents of a host object (a `Map`, a `Set`, a class instance) when a copy of it is made, as when a handler arm binds it.
````
details = ````markdown
A `HashMap` handed through a handler arm into a `Mutex` lost its buckets.
````

@ changed[]
area = "backends"
summary = ````markdown
A function listed in `exports` for the JavaScript backend may use a `Ref`, a `Weak`, a `Mutex`, an `Atomic` and `hash_seed`, and may spawn tasks that do.
````
details = ````markdown
Its row may hold `ref_new`, `ref_get`, `ref_set`, `weak_of`, `weak_get`, the `mutex_*` and `atomic_*` operations and `hash_seed`, which the instance answers as `Host::run` would; an instance of `spawn` (`spawn(u64)`); and a `spawn` whose task's row holds only these effects. A function whose row, or whose task's row, holds another host effect (`wall_clock`) is still an error.
````
